WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.331
Stannis Baratheon: My brother, Robert Baratheon,
had raised the banners of Storm's End, our

00:00:05.331 --> 00:00:09.920
ancestral castle, against the Mad King Aerys.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.370
Jon Arryn of the Vale and Eddard Stark of
the North stood with him, and Hoster Tully

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.500
of the Riverlands would join.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.831
But their lands were far from ours and separated
by the combined strength of the West, the

00:00:23.831 --> 00:00:27.859
Reach, and King's Landing itself.

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:30.010
Even Robert's own lords were against him.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:37.100
It was the hardest choice I've ever made:
my brother or my king, blood or honor.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.309
Aerys ruled by right of all the laws in Westeros.

00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:43.470
Everyone knew the price of defiance.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:49.760
But there are deeper, older laws: the younger
brother bows before the elder.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.180
I followed Robert.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:58.750
Early in the war, Mace Tyrell's indecisive
victory at Ashford cut Robert off from Storm's

00:00:58.750 --> 00:00:59.750
End.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:06.460
Instead of pursuing Robert, and risking his
record, Mace Tyrell turned east and laid siege

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.360
to our home.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:14.350
His vast army and navy encircled us and preventing
any resupply by land or sea.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.220
If a wagon tried to reach us, it was burned.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.930
If a ship tried to land, it was sunk.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.350
We were locked inside Storm's End to starve.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:26.961
But Robert had commanded me to hold the castle
no matter the cost.

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:31.869
He could ill afford to lose his ancient seat,
which had never fallen.

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:38.909
While Robert smashed Rhaegar on the Trident,
my men ate the dogs because the horses had

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:40.479
already been devoured.

00:01:40.479 --> 00:01:45.670
While the Lannisters sacked King's Landing,
we ate the rats.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:51.250
If the smuggler Davos had not slipped through
the Tyrell blockade with his onions, we'd

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:54.200
have eaten our own dead.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:02:01.530
But I held the castle until Lord Eddard remembered
us, and marched to lift the siege.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:09.119
The Tyrells didn't even put up a fight, and
Robert threw a feast to celebrate Lord Eddard's

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:10.410
"victory."

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:16.420
I was sent to the royal island stronghold
of Dragonstone to deal with Viserys and Daenerys,

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:18.510
the last surviving Targaryen children.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:24.650
Before I arrived, however, they had escaped
across the Narrow Sea.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.950
Robert was furious.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:34.780
He stripped me of Storm's End and gave it
to that prancing fool Renly, my younger brother.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.450
Davos Seaworth: Wars are not as good for smugglers
as you'd think.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:44.879
Every harbor fills with guards and inspectors,
and the seas fill with blockades and pirates

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:47.260
paid by each side to prey on the other.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:51.960
Though I had no love for the Mad King, I'd
grown up around the power of King's Landing.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:58.440
I figured this Robert Baratheon would end
as the other rebel lords: burned to ash.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.510
But he didn't.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.519
The North, the Riverlands, and the Vale joined
him.

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:06.909
And in the taverns, people drank to Robert's
health openly.

00:03:06.909 --> 00:03:08.620
"Brave fools," I thought.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.849
But I had a family who'd be left in the cold
if I lost my head.

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:19.690
When Mace Tyrell marched on Robert's home
at Storm's End, I spied the end of the rebellion.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:24.260
The castle was garrisoned by Robert's younger
brother Stannis and a small guard, and would

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.260
not hold out for long.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.620
When it fell, Robert would be homeless, and
his support would bleed away.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:33.530
This, I knew from experience.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.730
Months later, Stannis was still holding the
castle.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.409
Nobody cared.

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:45.230
But on voyages, I had seen what famine does;
and I thought of all those men in Storm's

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:49.260
End, who would die unmourned and forgotten.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.930
No better than Flea Bottom orphans.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:57.909
I told his wife, and myself, that I'd get
a high price for the onions and salt beef.

00:03:57.909 --> 00:04:02.470
In truth, I knew I'd be captured by the Tyrell
galleys or drowned.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.690
But I was too stubborn.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:10.129
Later that night, in the dark, in a tiny boat
with a black sail, I cursed myself and the

00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:13.310
moonlight as I waited for the tide to turn.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:19.190
When it did, the wind beat the sail so hard
I ripped it down, fearing the Tyrell ships

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.190
would hear.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.860
Luckily, they had grown lax.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:29.440
With muffled oars, alone, I steered my cargo
through the treacherous currents and snarls

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.090
of rock that gave Shipbreaker Bay its name.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:39.490
The waves finally carried me, soaked and near-blind
from seawater, through the mouth of the cavern

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.720
beneath the castle.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:45.889
Then Stannis Baratheon arrived.

00:04:45.889 --> 00:04:49.080
The siege had left him gaunt, but not weak,
never weak.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:55.750
He greeted me and accepted my onions with
cool courtesy, betraying no emotion even as

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.060
all wept.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:03.380
He doled out the food to his wife and each
of his men before he ate himself, a portion

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.400
no larger than any other.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:12.080
When he finally thanked me, I could see his
mind had already returned to the castle's

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.090
defense.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.770
His duty.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:19.680
After Aerys fell and Lord Stark lifted the
siege, Stannis summoned me.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:26.090
For my salvation of Storm's End, I was to
be granted a knighthood, a keep of my own,

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.639
and my son taken into Stannis's personal service.

00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:35.990
"Davos of Flea Bottom" had become "Ser Davos
of House Seaworth," and my son would serve

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.020
the king's own brother.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:44.620
But for my previous crimes as a smuggler,
I was to have the fingertips of one hand taken

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.050
off above the highest joint.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:51.490
Stannis held that I had flouted the laws of
the land for years, and a good act does not

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:52.750
wash out the bad.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:06:00.380
In one fell swoop, or five, Stannis gave my
son a future and my family a name that I could've

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.470
never imagined, nor earned, on my own.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:09.419
I still keep the finger bones in a bag around
my neck to remind me of what I was, and what

00:06:09.419 --> 00:06:12.130
I owe to Stannis.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:17.850
For during my many years as a smuggler, I
visited many ports, taverns, and back alleys,

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:22.479
and saw many things in this world, but never
justice.

00:06:22.479 --> 00:06:24.940
Until Stannis.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:28.630
Robert Baratheon: Rebellion!

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:35.780
The crimes of House Targaryen were too heinous
to go unanswered.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:42.070
The noble Houses of Baratheon, Stark, and
Arryn, united to oppose and overthrow the

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:45.680
line of the cursed dragon kings.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:52.419
While Ned Stark and Arryn secured an alliance
with the Tullys of Riverrun, I called the

00:06:52.419 --> 00:06:58.530
banners of Storm's End and rode out in force
against the Mad King and his minions.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:02.600
Gods, those were some battles!

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:08.010
Our first victory occurred at Summerhall where
I faced off against an army of dragon loyalists

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:12.460
and won three battles in a single day, three
in one day!

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.960
Seven hells, that was a glorious day!

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:22.350
We tried to take Ashford Castle in the Reach,
but the Tyrells beat us back.

00:07:22.350 --> 00:07:23.770
We had to regroup.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:31.310
My army was pursued north by Aerys's army
and took refuge in the Stoney Sept in the

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.310
Riverlands.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:37.650
When the Targaryen army entered the town,
the sept bells tolled, a signal to the townspeople

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:40.530
of the battle that was to come.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:46.419
As the Targaryens searched from house to house
for me, the combined forces of Ned Stark and

00:07:46.419 --> 00:07:48.740
the Tullys swept into the city.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:52.580
Gods, what a day that was!

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:56.660
It's now known as the Battle of the Bells.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:04.289
We overwhelmed the Mad King's forces and sent
them scampering back to King's Landing.

00:08:04.289 --> 00:08:09.900
Aerys's son, Rhaegar, who started the whole
damn thing, finally emerged from hiding in

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:12.961
the South and assembled his own army to face
us.

00:08:12.961 --> 00:08:19.360
As for the Mad King, he must have been pissing
himself.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.800
The battle that would decide the fate of the
Seven Kingdoms occurred at the crossing of

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.130
the Green Fork of the Trident river.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:32.890
Rhaegar commanded the royal host, which was
some forty thousand strong.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:39.750
My forces were outnumbered by nearly five
thousand men, but that didn't matter.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:46.940
They were fresh, but we were battle-hardened
and had justice on our side.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:50.630
As the battle raged around us, I faced off
with Rhaegar.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:56.140
The stag and the dragon right there in the
ford of the river.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:02.750
I fought with the fury of ten men, raining
blow after blow upon that vile prince before

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:05.800
burying my war hammer in his chest.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:11.450
I hit him so hard, the rubies on his armor
broke free, flinging them into the stream.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:14.769
They call it the Ruby Ford now.

00:09:14.769 --> 00:09:20.690
With that scum Rhaegar dead and the royal
army shattered, our next move was to make

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:22.270
for King's Landing.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:27.700
But I'd sustained a few wounds in the battle
and was unable to ride.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:33.810
I sent Ned Stark to the capital to face the
Mad King and make him pay for his crimes.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:40.070
Viserys Targaryen: The Targaryens, blood of
the dragon and the last of Old Valyria, were

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:45.800
loved by their subjects and admired far and
wide as the greatest dynasty in the history

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.050
of the western world.

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:53.380
But the peace and prosperity of nearly three
centuries of Targaryen rule were shattered

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:59.279
by the Usurper, Robert Baratheon, and his
band of traitors.

00:09:59.279 --> 00:10:03.930
House Baratheon owed its very existence to
the Targaryens.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:08.500
Was it not Aegon the Dragon, himself, who
elevated the bastard Orys Baratheon in the

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.750
War of Conquest?

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.240
And what of the Starks?

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.450
The Lannisters?

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:15.890
The Arryns of the Vale?

00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:21.670
All had been spared and allowed to keep their
lands when Aegon could easily have wiped them

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:22.720
out.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:29.800
Centuries later, the Usurper and his lackeys
repaid Aegon's benevolence with treachery.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:35.410
There are some who dare to claim Robert and
his allies had reason to rebel.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:40.019
They say the crown prince stole the Usurper's
lady love.

00:10:40.019 --> 00:10:46.820
They say my father, King Aerys, murdered Rickard
Stark and his son without just cause.

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:49.480
Whether these charges are true or not, it
doesn't matter!

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:53.140
The dragon answers to no one.

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:56.589
Aerys's good name has been besmirched in the
years since the rebellion.

00:10:56.589 --> 00:11:03.690
He has been called a dangerous madman, a monster,
a tyrant that brought his tragic end upon

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.280
himself.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.870
Lies!

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:10.940
My father was a victim of weaklings in his
council!

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:16.930
Lackwits who failed him in his hour of need,
and let the rebellion spin out of control!

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:19.700
But it was not enough.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.640
The royal army was crushed at the Battle of
the Trident.

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:28.670
It was there the valiant Rhaegar met Robert
in single combat, but the gods betrayed him,

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:33.360
and he perished by the Usurper's hand.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:39.180
As the Field of Fire had marked the end of
the Andals centuries before, the Battle of

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:43.500
the Trident seemed to herald the end of the
dragon kings.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:48.399
When word reached the capital of my brother
Rhaegar's death, my father Aerys moved to

00:11:48.399 --> 00:11:52.500
protect me, as I was the surviving heir to
the throne.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:57.649
He sent me to the island fortress of Dragonstone,
along with my mother, Queen Rhaella, who was

00:11:57.649 --> 00:12:00.110
great with child.

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:06.339
But as my father, my king, Aerys Targaryen,
prepared to defend his throne to the bitter

00:12:06.339 --> 00:12:11.171
end, little did he know of the horrors and
betrayals that awaited him and our family.

